{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Indus sign-sequence model — exploratory research notebook\n","\n","This notebook demonstrates a provisional model for interpreting selected Indus signs and sequences. Its readings and meanings are hypotheses for research, not verified translations or an accepted decipherment. The Indus script remains undeciphered. Any proposed relationship to Brahmi or other scripts needs independent, evidence-based evaluation.\n","\n","The model reflects a specific school of interpretation. Researchers interested in this approach are welcome to examine it; so are critics and scholars proposing alternatives. Please document evidence, uncertainty, and tests that could disconfirm a reading. A program's output is not evidence that its interpretation is correct.\n","\n","The current mappings below are retained as the model's assumptions. Add source citations and object/corpus identifiers before treating an input sequence as research data. This notebook runs locally: it does not request credentials, clone repositories, or upload data."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Data and logging\n","\n","The CSV uses the requested columns: `Timestamp`, `Seal_Identifier`, `Sign_Sequence`, `Decoded_Sanskrit`, and `Prashasanik_Meaning`. These names preserve compatibility with the earlier prototype; values are provisional model outputs. The notebook creates a local CSV if one does not exist and appends entries only when `decode_seal` is called. Review and cite data sources before sharing a log."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import csv\n","from datetime import datetime\n","from pathlib import Path\n","\n","class ExploratoryIndusModel:\n","    \"\"\"Prototype implementation of provisional mappings; not a validated decipherment.\"\"\"\n","\n","    def __init__(self, db_filename=\"indus_seals_database.csv\"):\n","        self.db_path = Path(db_filename)\n","        self.consonants = {\n","            '🏺': 'Ka', '𓏎': 'Kha', '𓏍': 'Ga', '𓎏': 'Ca', '𓎐': 'Cha',\n","            '𓏲': 'Ta', '🏹': 'Ta', '𓊍': 'Dha', '𓏏': 'Dha', '𓍢': 'Na',\n","            '🧍': 'Pa', '𓀜': 'Pha', '𓆛': 'Ma', '◯': 'Ra', '☉': 'Ra',\n","            '🌿': 'Sha', '𓇚': 'Sha'\n","        }\n","        if not self.db_path.exists():\n","            with self.db_path.open('w', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n","                csv.writer(f).writerow([\n","                    'Timestamp', 'Seal_Identifier', 'Sign_Sequence',\n","                    'Decoded_Sanskrit', 'Prashasanik_Meaning'\n","                ])\n","\n","    def decode_sequence(self, sequence_input):\n","        # These rules encode current model assumptions; they are not established readings.\n","        tokens = [token.strip() for token in sequence_input.split('+') if token.strip()]\n","        decoded = []\n","        if tokens and tokens[0] in ('𓎦', '37'):\n","            decoded.append('Mahā')\n","            tokens = tokens[1:]\n","\n","        i = 0\n","        while i < len(tokens):\n","            token = tokens[i]\n","            final = i == len(tokens) - 1\n","            if final and token in ('𓆛', '99'):\n","                decoded.append('m'); i += 1; continue\n","            if final and token in ('𓆜', '162'):\n","                decoded.append('asya'); i += 1; continue\n","            if final and token in ('𓆟', '99_wing'):\n","                decoded.append('asti'); i += 1; continue\n","\n","            if token in ('𓀠', '311_R') and '⚙' in tokens:\n","                decoded.append('Bhārata')\n","                tokens.remove('⚙')\n","            elif token in ('⚙', '245_S'):\n","                if i + 1 < len(tokens) and tokens[i + 1] in ('⚙', '245_S'):\n","                    decoded.append('Rājarāja'); i += 1\n","                else:\n","                    decoded.append('Rāja')\n","            elif token in ('🌿', '𓇚') and i + 1 < len(tokens) and tokens[i + 1] in ('𓀜', '311_W'):\n","                decoded.append('Śubha'); i += 1\n","            elif token in ('𓍢', 'hook') and i + 1 < len(tokens) and tokens[i + 1] in ('𓀜', '311_W'):\n","                decoded.append('Lābha'); i += 1\n","            else:\n","                decoded.append(self.consonants.get(token, token))\n","            i += 1\n","\n","        text = '-'.join(decoded).replace('-m', 'm').replace('-asya', 'asya').replace('-asti', 'asti')\n","        # Keep interpretations explicitly provisional in the output.\n","        interpretation = 'Unassigned — provisional model output; requires evidence and review'\n","        if 'Bhārata' in text:\n","            interpretation = 'Proposed jurisdictional reading — unvalidated model output'\n","        elif 'Rājarāja' in text or 'Mahā' in text:\n","            interpretation = 'Proposed sovereign reading — unvalidated model output'\n","        elif 'Śubha' in text or 'Lābha' in text:\n","            interpretation = 'Proposed civic/trade reading — unvalidated model output'\n","        return text, interpretation\n","\n","    def decode_seal(self, seal_id, sequence_input, log=True):\n","        decoded, interpretation = self.decode_sequence(sequence_input)\n","        if log:\n","            with self.db_path.open('a', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n","                csv.writer(f).writerow([\n","                    datetime.now().isoformat(timespec='seconds'), seal_id,\n","                    sequence_input, decoded, interpretation\n","                ])\n","        return decoded, interpretation\n","\n","model = ExploratoryIndusModel()\n","\n","# Example only: replace with a documented sign sequence and cite its source.\n","example_decoding = model.decode_seal(\n","    seal_id='EXAMPLE — replace with source identifier',\n","    sequence_input='𓎦+311_R+⚙+𓆜',\n","    log=False,  # Do not log the illustrative example as archaeological data.\n","]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["print('Provisional model output:', example_decoding[0])\n","print('Interpretation status:', example_decoding[1])\n","\n","# For a documented entry, call model.decode_seal(identifier, sequence, log=True).\n","# This writes only to the local CSV file; it does not upload or publish it."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Limitations and next research steps\n","\n","The mapping table and rules are inherited from an earlier prototype and are not accompanied here by a validated sign list, a complete corpus, or sufficient source citations. They should be checked against documented inscriptions and relevant scholarship. Sign identification, reading direction, segmentation, phonetic values, language, and historical relationships are all open questions.\n","\n","For a useful research contribution, record the object/corpus identifier, edition or image source, sign sequence and direction, transcription decisions, proposed reading, uncertainty, and a test that could count against the interpretation. Do not treat the sample sequence or generated CSV output as a genuine inscription or established translation."]}]}